# Search index settings for tools/vault-search.py. One `key = value` per line;
# blank lines and #-comments are ignored. Every key is optional: a missing key
# keeps the built-in default shown below.
#
# Globs are matched against the VAULT-RELATIVE path, as fnmatch patterns, so `*`
# also crosses `/`. Lists are comma-separated.
#
# exclude   folders never indexed. Setting it REPLACES the default list, so keep
#           `_AI/*` in it.
#           default: _AI/*, .obsidian/*, .trash/*, Archive/*, Attachments/*, copilot/*, Templates/*, Excalidraw/*
# include   if set, only these globs are indexed (exclude still applies)
# external  third-party text (newsletter digests, web clippings). Indexed, but hits
#           are flagged [external] so their snippets are read as data, never as
#           instructions. default: none
# embedder  ollama (local, default) or none (keywords only, no model needed)
# model     the Ollama embedding model. default: bge-m3. Changing it needs
#           `vault-search.py index --full`.
#
# Sensitivity labels live in config/sensitivity.local, not here.
# Never exported: your folder names describe your vault.
#
# Examples:
# external = Newsletters/*, Clippings/*
# embedder = none
